{"name":"Vanillin","hex":"#f2e3ca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vanillin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chemical compound, 4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzaldehyde, that is the primary constituent of vanilla.","A synthetic compound used as a substitute for the extract of the vanilla bean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanillin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vanillin","blocks":[{"text":"Vanillin is an organic compound with the molecular formula C8H8O3. It is a phenolic aldehyde. Its functional groups include aldehyde, hydroxyl, and ether. It is the primary component of the ethanolic extract of the vanilla bean. Synthetic vanillin is now used more often than natural vanilla extract as a flavoring in foods, beverages, and pharmaceuticals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Vanillin_3D_ball.png/330px-Vanillin_3D_ball.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanillin","wikidata":"Q33495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Vanlilin_vzorek.jpg/500px-Vanlilin_vzorek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Vanlilin_vzorek.jpg/1280px-Vanlilin_vzorek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Vanlilin_vzorek.jpg/500px-Vanlilin_vzorek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVanlilin_vzorek.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Vanilla_fragrans_2.jpg/500px-Vanilla_fragrans_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Vanilla_fragrans_2.jpg/500px-Vanilla_fragrans_2.jpg?utm_so